Description: Fcitx5 mixed Bopomofo/English input without mode switching
 Ari IME is a Fcitx5 input method for Traditional Chinese that lets you type
 Bopomofo (注音) and English together without switching modes. Every key first
 shows as itself; keys only become Chinese once they form a complete, toned
 注音 syllable (for example "su3" becomes 你). The whole pre-edit may freely
 mix English and Chinese in any order (for example "acer螢幕") and is only sent
 to the application on Enter.
 .
 Conversion, phrasing and per-user learning are provided by libchewing.
